# ── v4/v5 LOD levels: the count/bytes split (generator version 2) ────────────
# The LOD section was the ONLY place in the format storing a count and its byte
# size as INDEPENDENT fields — everywhere else the bytes are derived from the
# count, so the two cannot disagree. AssetService builds
# `Mesh lm(lvb, lib, lvl.indexCount)`, handing that count to bgfx as a draw
# range, so a level declaring more indices than it ships is a GPU read off the
# end of the buffer. The section also shipped entirely unfuzzed: buildPlausible
# only ever emitted v2, so no case reached it.
#
# These seeds were produced by the InflateLod* corruptions and each one FAILED
# before the loader cross-checked count*stride == bytes and clamped every level
# range to the level's own index count.
